# Spike — lossless list boundaries
Purpose/mode: bounded spike on request.txt:1; ordinary decision question, no initiative or feature shipment needed. Canonical discovery found no packs (trace 9).

## Source pins and knowledge limits
HEAD above (trace 3). Product/probe sources clean; pre-existing dirty wiki/.okf/fingerprints.json and last-index.json diffs are trace 5; no staged changes (6). Hashes in source-pins.json pin all supplied inputs.
Knowledge validation has 0 errors/0 warnings (10), status says fresh (11), but src/list.ts anchor is “not yet baselined” (12). Python-only scanner and HEAD stamp do not verify dirty TypeScript/Markdown content. Metadata is not refreshed; inspected source decides.

## Scope and Out-of-scope
In: list(notes) output representation and unrestricted string id/title boundaries; run supplied diagnostic and, if it is erroneous, corrected throwaway boundary probe.
Out: shipping exporter, changing list or supplied diagnostic, new dependency/service, storage migration, performance survey, deployment and owner actions.

## The question
Q-E1 (experiment): Can the existing tab-separated list renderer represent ids/titles containing actual tabs and newlines without losing field/record boundaries? It blocks the bulk-export reuse design decision. Planner owns the decision; local counterexample resolves the representation question.

## Timebox and stop conditions — declared before any experiment
Five minutes beginning at the actual clock recorded in declaration.json, not the start of prior source reads. Stop as soon as a deciding counterexample is captured, the question is otherwise answered or the deadline expires.
Kill: unequal note arrays with identical output bytes disprove lossless representation; import/runtime error without deciding witness requires bounded probe repair; deadline ends exploration as inconclusive.
No experiment has run at declaration. Reading previous-probe.ts:1–5 was grounding. It asserts equality but its title appears to use literal backslash sequences; the assertion itself supplies no result.

## Method
Run previous-probe.ts unchanged once and capture exit/stdout/stderr. A collision message is not trusted without output equality.
If it errors without a deciding witness, run analysis/boundary-probe.ts (marked throwaway). Construct real TAB=codepoint 9 and LF=10, verify ordinary/empty behavior, capture unequal arrays and output bytes, then assert identical outputs. Include title, id and field-boundary cases in the single deciding run. Abort execution if the declared deadline is already past.
Retain first failures; separate diagnostic mistakes from subject evidence. Do not implement alternative serialization.

## Findings and outcome
Not established yet at declaration; record a dated result supplement after observing command output. No earlier scratch session or consent history is reconstructed.

## Assumptions
A1: id/title permit arbitrary strings as src/list.ts:1 declares; blast radius export suitability; validation trigger is a later accepted input restriction.
A2: “without losing record boundaries” requires distinguishable records from output alone, without a separate framing channel; blast radius bulk export decision; validation trigger is evidence of such a channel.
No upstream API/event/database/provider/auth boundary exists in the supplied slice; CLI dispatch is absent and production use unknown.

## Open questions and handoff
Q-E1 above is the sole active experiment. A later design question Q-D1 asks what framing/escaping format or input restriction is acceptable if reuse fails; planner + owner resolves it before a bulk-export implementation plan. It does not block running this spike.
Artifacts: this declaration/report, declaration.json, source-pins.json, throwaway boundary-probe.ts, later result supplement and checks.md. No candidate FRs or machine requirements: the user asked a diagnostic decision, not a new capability.
Next: execute the declared method within timebox and report evidence, answer/confidence, residual questions and observed timing. Planned checks are not actual results. No owner interaction or independent review/scoring.
